---
import { getCollection } from "astro:content";
import Doc from "../../../layouts/Doc.astro";
import Badge from "../../../components/Badge.astro";
import ReviewTrail from "../../../components/ReviewTrail.astro";
import { strategyData, sessionLabel, MIN_ELIGIBLE_TRADES } from "../../../lib/data";
import { F2_VERDICTS } from "../../../data/verdicts";
import { usd, int, date, tone } from "../../../lib/format";

export async function getStaticPaths() {
  const all = await getCollection("strategies", (s) => s.data.stage === "tested");
  return all.flatMap((entry) => (entry.data.dataKey ? [{ params: { slug: entry.id }, props: { entry, key: entry.data.dataKey } }] : []));
}
const { entry, key } = Astro.props;
const data = strategyData(key);
const f1 = data.features.f1;
const f2 = data.features.f2;
const verdicts = F2_VERDICTS[key] ?? {};
const toc = [
  { depth: 2, slug: "protocol", text: "Protocol" },
  { depth: 2, slug: "exposure", text: "Exposure to reserved data" },
  { depth: 2, slug: "runs", text: "Every run" },
  { depth: 2, slug: "reviews", text: "Reviews" },
  { depth: 2, slug: "sources", text: "Source files" },
];
---
<Doc title={`${entry.data.title}: evidence`} description={`Protocol, exposure history, every run and the reviews behind ${entry.data.title}.`} toc={toc}>
  <Fragment slot="head">
    <p class="crumbs"><a href="/strategies/">Strategies</a> / <a href={`/strategies/${entry.id}/`}>{entry.data.title}</a> /</p>
    <h1>Evidence and run history</h1>
    <p class="lede">Everything behind the numbers on the strategy page: what was decided before testing, every
    search run with its verdict, what touched the reserved data, and who checked what.</p>
  </Fragment>
  <div class="prose wide">
    <h2 id="protocol">Protocol</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Feature 1:</strong> {f1.grid_size.join(", ")} settings per session, each run over the full data
      ({date(Object.values(f1.variants)[0].scenarios["0"].period_start)} to {date(Object.values(f1.variants)[0].scenarios["0"].period_end)}).
      The winner is the highest net profit at 0 ticks, then rerun at 1 and 2 ticks.</li>
      {f2 && <li><strong>Feature 2:</strong> development data only (before 1 Jan 2024). Hypotheses, objective and trial budget were
      written down before the first run. Objective: net profit plus open P&amp;L at 1 tick, with at least {MIN_ELIGIBLE_TRADES}
      closed trades. {int(f2.total_trials)} search trials in total, {int(f2.total_engine_evaluations)} engine runs logged.</li>}
      <li><strong>Feature 3:</strong> not built yet.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2 id="exposure">Exposure to reserved data</h2>
    <p>Reserved means "not used to pick settings". These are the known exceptions, copied from the run ledger:</p>
    <ul>
      {f2?.lineage.map((n) => <li>{n}</li>)}
      {f2?.manual_looks.map((m) => <li><span class="mono">{date(m.time_utc)}</span> · {m.evaluations} engine runs · {m.note}</li>)}
    </ul>
    <p>So 2024+ is reserved, but it is not a clean out-of-sample test. Feature 3 has to count this.</p>

    <h2 id="runs">Every run</h2>
    {f2 && (
      <div class="table-scroll">
        <table class="data">
          <caption class="sr-only">All feature-2 runs</caption>
          <thead>
            <tr><th scope="col">Run</th><th scope="col" class="num">Trials</th><th scope="col" class="num">Eligible</th><th scope="col" class="num">Engine runs</th><th scope="col" class="num">Net 0 / 1 / 2 ticks</th><th scope="col">Verdict</th></tr>
          </thead>
          <tbody>
            {f2.runs.map((r) => (
              <tr>
                <th scope="row"><span class="mono run">{r.run_id}</span><span class="sub">{sessionLabel(r.variant)} · {r.sampler} · seed {r.seed} · trial #{r.source_trial} · {date(r.time_utc)}</span></th>
                <td class="num">{int(r.trials)}{r.duplicates > 0 && <span class="sub">{r.duplicates} repeats</span>}</td>
                <td class="num">{int(r.eligible)}</td>
                <td class="num">{int(r.evaluations)}</td>
                <td class="num">{(["0", "1", "2"] as const).map((k, i) => <><span class={tone(r.scenarios[k].net_profit)}>{usd(r.scenarios[k].net_profit, { cents: false })}</span>{i < 2 && <br />}</>)}</td>
                <td><Badge tone={verdicts[r.run_id]?.verdict === "candidate" ? "done" : "rejected"}>{verdicts[r.run_id]?.verdict ?? "none"}</Badge></td>
              </tr>
            ))}
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>
    )}
    <p>"Eligible" means the trial had at least {MIN_ELIGIBLE_TRADES} closed trades. Each trial runs the engine at 0, 1 and 2 ticks, and
    neighbour checks add more runs, so engine runs are about three times the trials.</p>

    <h2 id="reviews">Reviews</h2>
    <ReviewTrail reviews={entry.data.reviews} />

    <h2 id="sources">Source files</h2>
    <p>The numbers on this site are copied from these tester outputs by an exporter that never recomputes them.
    Exported {date(data.generated_utc)}, format version {data.export_version}. SHA-256 shown in short.</p>
    <div class="table-scroll">
      <table class="data src">
        <thead><tr><th scope="col">File</th><th scope="col">SHA-256</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
          {data.sources.map((s) => <tr><td class="mono">{s.path}</td><td class="mono">{s.sha256.slice(0, 16)}…</td></tr>)}
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
  </div>
</Doc>
<style>
  .crumbs {
    font-size: 0.875rem;
    color: var(--ink-3);
    margin-bottom: 1rem;
  }
  .crumbs a {
    color: var(--ink-2);
    text-decoration: none;
  }
  .lede {
    margin-top: 1rem;
    max-width: 60ch;
    font-size: 1.125rem;
    color: var(--ink-2);
  }
  .wide {
    max-width: none;
  }
  .wide > :global(p),
  .wide > :global(ul),
  .wide > :global(h2) {
    max-width: var(--measure);
  }
  .wide > :global(h2) {
    margin-top: 3.5rem;
  }
  .wide > :global(h2:first-child) {
    margin-top: 0;
  }
  .run {
    font-size: 0.8125rem;
  }
  .sub {
    display: block;
    font-size: 0.75rem;
    font-weight: 400;
    color: var(--ink-3);
  }
  .src td {
    font-size: 0.75rem;
  }
</style>
